#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson shows the complete workflow for some variational approaches and describes how they can be modified."
msgstr "Pelajaran ini menunjukkan aliran kerja lengkap untuk beberapa pendekatan variasi dan menerangkan cara ia boleh diubah suai."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instances and extensions"
msgstr "Contoh dan perluasan"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell: ignore disp SSVQE's forall */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell: ignore disp SSVQE's forall */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This chapter will cover several quantum variational algorithms, including\n"
msgstr "Bab ini akan merangkumi beberapa algoritma variasi kuantum, termasuk\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Variational Quantum Eigensolver (VQE)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.3061)\n"
msgstr "[Variational Quantum Eigensolver (VQE)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.3061)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Subspace Search VQE (SSVQE)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.09434)\n"
msgstr "[Subspace Search VQE (SSVQE)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.09434)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Variational Quantum Deflation (VQD)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08138)\n"
msgstr "[Variational Quantum Deflation (VQD)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08138)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Quantum Sampling Regression (QSR)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.02338)\n"
msgstr "[Quantum Sampling Regression (QSR)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.02338)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By using these algorithms, we will learn about several design ideas that can be incorporated into custom variational algorithms, such as weights, penalties, over-sampling, and under-sampling. We encourage you to experiment with these concepts and share your findings with the community.\n"
msgstr "Dengan menggunakan algoritma-algoritma ini, kita akan mempelajari beberapa idea reka bentuk yang boleh digabungkan ke dalam algoritma variasi tersuai, seperti pemberat, penalti, over-sampling, dan under-sampling. Kami menggalakkan anda untuk bereksperimen dengan konsep-konsep ini dan berkongsi penemuan anda dengan komuniti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Qiskit patterns framework applies to all these algorithms - but we will explicitly call out the steps only in the first example.\n"
msgstr "Rangka kerja corak Qiskit terpakai untuk semua algoritma ini — tetapi kita hanya akan menyebut langkah-langkah secara eksplisit dalam contoh pertama sahaja.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Variational Quantum Eigensolver (VQE) {#variational-quantum-eigensolver-vqe}"
msgstr "Variational Quantum Eigensolver (VQE) {#variational-quantum-eigensolver-vqe}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[VQE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.3061) is one of the most widely used variational quantum algorithms, setting up a template for other algorithms to build upon.\n"
msgstr "[VQE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.3061) adalah salah satu algoritma kuantum variasi yang paling banyak digunakan, membentuk templat untuk algoritma-algoritma lain dibina di atasnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing how VQE uses the reference state and ansatz to estimate a cost function, and then iterate using variational parameters.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-vqe.svg)\n"
msgstr "![A diagram showing how VQE uses the reference state and ansatz to estimate a cost function, and then iterate using variational parameters.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-vqe.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout}"
msgstr "Susun atur teori {#theoretical-layout}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "VQE's layout is simple:\n"
msgstr "Susun atur VQE adalah mudah:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare reference operators $U_R$\n"
msgstr "Sediakan operator rujukan $U_R$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We start from the state $|0\\rangle$ and go to the reference state $|\\rho\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "Kita bermula dari keadaan $|0\\rangle$ dan pergi ke keadaan rujukan $|\\rho\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply the variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to create an ansatz $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$\n"
msgstr "Gunakan bentuk variasi $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ untuk mencipta ansatz $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We go from the state $|\\rho\\rangle$ to $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})|\\rho\\rangle = |\\psi(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "Kita pergi dari keadaan $|\\rho\\rangle$ kepada $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})|\\rho\\rangle = |\\psi(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bootstrap at $i=0$ if we have a similar problem (typically found via classical simulation or sampling)\n"
msgstr "Bootstrap pada $i=0$ jika kita mempunyai masalah yang serupa (biasanya ditemui melalui simulasi atau pensampelan klasik)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each optimizer will be bootstrapped differently, resulting in an initial set of parameter vectors $\\Theta_0 := \\\\{ {\\vec\\theta_{0,j} | j \\in \\mathcal{J}_\\text{opt}^0} \\\\}$ (for example, from an initial point $\\vec\\theta_0$).\n"
msgstr "Setiap pengoptimum akan di-bootstrap secara berbeza, menghasilkan set vektor parameter awal $\\Theta_0 := \\\\{ {\\vec\\theta_{0,j} | j \\in \\mathcal{J}_\\text{opt}^0} \\\\}$ (contohnya, dari titik awal $\\vec\\theta_0$).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate the cost function $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ for all prepared states on a quantum computer.\n"
msgstr "Nilaikan fungsi kos $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ untuk semua keadaan yang disediakan pada komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use a classical optimizer to select the next set of parameters $\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan pengoptimum klasik untuk memilih set parameter seterusnya $\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat the process until convergence is reached.\n"
msgstr "Ulang proses sehingga penumpuan dicapai.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is a simple classical optimization loop where we evaluate the cost function. Some optimizers may require multiple evaluations to calculate a gradient, determine the next iteration, or assess convergence.\n"
msgstr "Ini adalah gelung pengoptimuman klasik mudah di mana kita menilai fungsi kos. Sesetengah pengoptimum mungkin memerlukan pelbagai penilaian untuk mengira kecerunan, menentukan lelaran seterusnya, atau menilai penumpuan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here's the example for the following observable:\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah contoh untuk observable berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{O}_1 = 2 II - 2 XX + 3 YY - 3 ZZ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{O}_1 = 2 II - 2 XX + 3 YY - 3 ZZ,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation {#implementation}"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan {#implementation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/extracted-outputs/db20526e-48d4-44eb-9d2b-6c5d2ce5777e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/extracted-outputs/db20526e-48d4-44eb-9d2b-6c5d2ce5777e-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can use this cost function to calculate optimal parameters\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh menggunakan fungsi kos ini untuk mengira parameter optimum\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will select the least-busy backend, and import the necessary components from `qiskit_ibm_runtime`.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan memilih Backend yang paling tidak sibuk, dan mengimport komponen yang diperlukan dari `qiskit_ibm_runtime`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will transpile the circuit using the preset pass manager with optimization level 3, and we will apply the corresponding layout to the observable.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan men-transpil Circuit menggunakan preset pass manager dengan tahap pengoptimuman 3, dan kita akan menggunakan susun atur yang sepadan kepada observable.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using IBM Quantum primitives {#step-3-execute-using-ibm-quantum-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif IBM Quantum {#step-3-execute-using-ibm-quantum-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We are now ready to run our calculation on IBM Quantum&reg; hardware. Because the cost function minimization is highly iterative, we will start a Runtime session. This way, we will only have to wait in a queue once. Once the job begins running, each iteration with updates to parameters will run immediately.\n"
msgstr "Kita kini bersedia untuk menjalankan pengiraan kita pada perkakasan IBM Quantum&reg;. Oleh kerana pengecilan fungsi kos sangat berulang, kita akan memulakan Session Runtime. Dengan cara ini, kita hanya perlu menunggu dalam giliran sekali sahaja. Setelah kerja mula berjalan, setiap lelaran dengan kemas kini parameter akan berjalan serta-merta.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process, return result in classical format {#step-4-post-process-return-result-in-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses, kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik {#step-4-post-process-return-result-in-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can see that the minimization routine successfully terminated, meaning we reached the default tolerance of the COBYLA classical optimizer. If we require a more precise result, we can specify a smaller tolerance. This may indeed be the case, since the result was several percent off compared to the result obtained by the simulator above.\n"
msgstr "Kita dapat melihat bahawa rutin pengecilan berjaya ditamatkan, bermakna kita telah mencapai tolerans lalai pengoptimum klasik COBYLA. Jika kita memerlukan hasil yang lebih tepat, kita boleh menentukan tolerans yang lebih kecil. Ini mungkin memang berlaku, memandangkan hasilnya berbeza beberapa peratus berbanding dengan hasil yang diperoleh oleh simulator di atas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The value of x obtained is the current best guess for the parameters that minimize the cost function. If iterating to obtain a higher precision, those values should be used in place of the x0 initially used (a vector of ones).\n"
msgstr "Nilai x yang diperoleh adalah tekaan terbaik semasa untuk parameter yang meminimumkan fungsi kos. Jika berulang untuk mendapatkan ketepatan yang lebih tinggi, nilai-nilai tersebut harus digunakan sebagai ganti x0 yang digunakan pada mulanya (vektor satu).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we note that the function was evaluated 96 times in the process of optimization. That might be different from the number of optimization steps, since some optimizers require multiple function evaluations in a single step, such as when estimating a gradient.\n"
msgstr "Akhirnya, kita perhatikan bahawa fungsi itu dinilai sebanyak 96 kali dalam proses pengoptimuman. Itu mungkin berbeza daripada bilangan langkah pengoptimuman, kerana sesetengah pengoptimum memerlukan pelbagai penilaian fungsi dalam satu langkah, seperti ketika menganggar kecerunan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Subspace Search VQE (SSVQE) {#subspace-search-vqe-ssvqe}"
msgstr "Subspace Search VQE (SSVQE) {#subspace-search-vqe-ssvqe}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[SSVQE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.09434) is a variant of VQE that allows obtaining the first $k$ eigenvalues of an observable $\\hat{H}$ with eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, where $N\\geq k$. Without loss of generality, we assume that $\\lambda_0<\\lambda_1<...<\\lambda_{N-1}$. SSVQE introduces a new idea by adding weights to help prioritize optimizing for the term with the largest weight.\n"
msgstr "[SSVQE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.09434) adalah varian VQE yang membolehkan mendapatkan $k$ nilai eigen pertama bagi observable $\\hat{H}$ dengan nilai eigen $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, di mana $N\\geq k$. Tanpa kehilangan keumuman, kita andaikan bahawa $\\lambda_0<\\lambda_1<...<\\lambda_{N-1}$. SSVQE memperkenalkan idea baharu dengan menambah pemberat untuk membantu mengutamakan pengoptimuman bagi sebutan dengan pemberat terbesar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing how subspace-search VQE uses the components of variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-ssvqe.svg)\n"
msgstr "![A diagram showing how subspace-search VQE uses the components of variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-ssvqe.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To implement this algorithm, we need $k$ mutually orthogonal reference states $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, meaning $\\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ for $j,l<k$. These states can be constructed using Pauli operators. The cost function of this algorithm is then:\n"
msgstr "Untuk melaksanakan algoritma ini, kita memerlukan $k$ keadaan rujukan yang saling ortogon $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, bermakna $\\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ untuk $j,l<k$. Keadaan-keadaan ini boleh dibina menggunakan operator Pauli. Fungsi kos algoritma ini kemudian adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{\\theta})\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{\\theta})\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\rho_j | U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})\\hat{H} U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\rho_j | U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})\\hat{H} U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $w_j$ is an arbitrary positive number such that if $j<l<k$ then $w_j>w_l$, and $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})$ is the user-defined variational form.\n"
msgstr "di mana $w_j$ adalah nombor positif sewenang-wenangnya sedemikian sehingga jika $j<l<k$ maka $w_j>w_l$, dan $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})$ adalah bentuk variasi yang ditentukan pengguna.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The SSVQE algorithm relies on the fact that eigenstates corresponding to different eigenvalues are mutually orthogonal. Specifically, the inner product of $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle$ and $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l\\rangle$ can be expressed as:\n"
msgstr "Algoritma SSVQE bergantung pada fakta bahawa keadaan eigen yang sepadan dengan nilai eigen yang berbeza adalah saling ortogon. Khususnya, hasil darab dalam $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle$ dan $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l\\rangle$ boleh dinyatakan sebagai:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\rho_j | U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l \\rangle\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\rho_j | U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l \\rangle\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\langle \\rho_j | I |\\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\langle \\rho_j | I |\\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\delta_{jl}\n"
msgstr "& = \\delta_{jl}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first equality holds because $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})$ is a quantum operator and is therefore unitary. The last equality holds because of the orthogonality of the reference states $|\\rho_j\\rangle$. The fact that orthogonality is preserved through unitary transformations is deeply related to the principle of conservation of information, as expressed in quantum information science. Under this view, non-unitary transformations represent processes where information is either lost or injected.\n"
msgstr "Kesamaan pertama berlaku kerana $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})$ adalah operator kuantum dan oleh itu adalah unitary. Kesamaan terakhir berlaku kerana ortogonaliti keadaan rujukan $|\\rho_j\\rangle$. Fakta bahawa ortogonaliti dipelihara melalui transformasi unitary berkait rapat dengan prinsip pemuliharaan maklumat, seperti yang dinyatakan dalam sains maklumat kuantum. Dari pandangan ini, transformasi bukan-unitary mewakili proses di mana maklumat sama ada hilang atau disuntik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Weights $w_j$ help ensure that all the states are eigenstates. If the weights are sufficiently different, the term with the largest weight (that is, $w_0$) will be given priority during optimization over the others. As a result, the resulting state $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_0 \\rangle$ will become the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_0$. Because $\\{ U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$ are mutually orthogonal, the remaining states will be orthogonal to it and, therefore, contained in the subspace corresponding to the eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Pemberat $w_j$ membantu memastikan semua keadaan adalah keadaan eigen. Jika pemberat cukup berbeza, sebutan dengan pemberat terbesar (iaitu, $w_0$) akan diberi keutamaan semasa pengoptimuman berbanding yang lain. Akibatnya, keadaan yang terhasil $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_0 \\rangle$ akan menjadi keadaan eigen yang sepadan dengan $\\lambda_0$. Kerana $\\{ U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$ adalah saling ortogon, keadaan-keadaan selebihnya akan ortogon kepadanya dan, oleh itu, terkandung dalam subruang yang sepadan dengan nilai eigen $\\{\\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying the same argument to the rest of the terms, the next priority would then be the term with weight $w_1$, so $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_1 \\rangle$ would be the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_1$, and the other terms would be contained in the eigenspace of $\\{\\lambda_2,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan hujah yang sama untuk selebihnya sebutan-sebutan, keutamaan seterusnya ialah sebutan dengan pemberat $w_1$, jadi $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_1 \\rangle$ akan menjadi keadaan eigen yang sepadan dengan $\\lambda_1$, dan sebutan-sebutan lain akan terkandung dalam ruang eigen bagi $\\{\\lambda_2,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By reasoning inductively, we deduce that $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j \\rangle$ will be an approximate eigenstate of $\\lambda_j$ for $0\\leq j < k$.\n"
msgstr "Dengan penaakulan secara aruhan, kita simpulkan bahawa $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j \\rangle$ akan menjadi keadaan eigen anggaran bagi $\\lambda_j$ untuk $0\\leq j < k$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout-1}"
msgstr "Susun atur teori {#theoretical-layout-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SSVQE's can be summarized as follows:\n"
msgstr "SSVQE boleh diringkaskan seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare several reference states by applying a unitary U_R to k different computational basis states\n"
msgstr "Sediakan beberapa keadaan rujukan dengan menggunakan unitary U_R kepada k keadaan asas pengiraan yang berbeza\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "This algorithm requires the usage of $k$ mutually orthogonal reference states $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, such that $\\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ for $j,l<k$.\n"
msgstr "Algoritma ini memerlukan penggunaan $k$ keadaan rujukan yang saling ortogon $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, sedemikian sehingga $\\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ untuk $j,l<k$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply the variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to each reference state, resulting in the following ansatz $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan bentuk variasi $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ kepada setiap keadaan rujukan, menghasilkan ansatz berikut $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bootstrap at $i=0$ if a similar problem is available (usually found via classical simulation or sampling).\n"
msgstr "Bootstrap pada $i=0$ jika masalah yang serupa tersedia (biasanya ditemui melalui simulasi atau pensampelan klasik).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate the cost function $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ for all prepared states on a quantum computer.\n"
msgstr "Nilaikan fungsi kos $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ untuk semua keadaan yang disediakan pada komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "This can be separated into calculating the expectation value for an observable $\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ and multiplying that result by $w_j$.\n"
msgstr "Ini boleh dipisahkan kepada pengiraan nilai jangkaan bagi observable $\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ dan darab keputusan itu dengan $w_j$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Afterward, the cost function returns the sum of all weighted expectation values.\n"
msgstr "Selepas itu, fungsi kos mengembalikan jumlah semua nilai jangkaan berpemberat.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use a classical optimizer to determine the next set of parameters $\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan pengoptimum klasik untuk menentukan set parameter seterusnya $\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat the above steps until convergence is achieved.\n"
msgstr "Ulang langkah-langkah di atas sehingga penumpuan dicapai.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You will be reconstructing SSVQE's cost function in the assessment, but we have the following snippet to motivate your solution:\n"
msgstr "Anda akan membina semula fungsi kos SSVQE dalam penilaian, tetapi kami mempunyai petikan berikut untuk memotivasikan penyelesaian anda:\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Variational Quantum Deflation (VQD) {#variational-quantum-deflation-vqd}"
msgstr "Variational Quantum Deflation (VQD) {#variational-quantum-deflation-vqd}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[VQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08138) is an iterative method that extends VQE to obtain the first $k$ eigenvalues of an observable $\\hat{H}$ with eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, where $N\\geq k$, instead of only the first. For the rest of this section, we will assume, without loss of generality, that $\\lambda_0\\leq\\lambda_1\\leq...\\leq\\lambda_{N-1}$. VQD introduces the notion of a penalty cost to guide the optimization process.\n"
msgstr "[VQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08138) adalah kaedah berulang yang melanjutkan VQE untuk mendapatkan $k$ nilai eigen pertama bagi observable $\\hat{H}$ dengan nilai eigen $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, di mana $N\\geq k$, bukan hanya yang pertama sahaja. Untuk selebihnya bahagian ini, kita akan andaikan, tanpa kehilangan keumuman, bahawa $\\lambda_0\\leq\\lambda_1\\leq...\\leq\\lambda_{N-1}$. VQD memperkenalkan konsep kos penalti untuk membimbing proses pengoptimuman.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A diagram showing how VQD uses the components of a variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-vqd.svg)\n"
"VQD introduces a penalty term, denoted as $\\beta$, to balance the contribution of each overlap term to the cost. This penalty term serves to penalize the optimization process if orthogonality is not achieved. We impose this constraint because the eigenstates of an observable, or a Hermitian operator, corresponding to different eigenvalues are always mutually orthogonal, or can be made to be so in the case of degeneracy or repeated eigenvalues. Thus, by enforcing orthogonality with the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_0$, we are effectively optimizing over the subspace that corresponds to the rest of the eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2,..., \\lambda_{N-1}\\}$. Here, $\\lambda_1$ is the lowest eigenvalue from the rest of the eigenvalues and, therefore, the optimal solution of the new problem can be obtained using the variational theorem.\n"
msgstr ""
"![A diagram showing how VQD uses the components of a variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-vqd.svg)\n"
"VQD memperkenalkan sebutan penalti, ditandai sebagai $\\beta$, untuk mengimbangi sumbangan setiap sebutan pertindanan kepada kos. Sebutan penalti ini berfungsi untuk menghukum proses pengoptimuman jika ortogonaliti tidak dicapai. Kita mengenakan kekangan ini kerana keadaan eigen bagi observable, atau operator Hermitian, yang sepadan dengan nilai eigen yang berbeza sentiasa saling ortogon, atau boleh dibuat sedemikian dalam kes keterulangan atau nilai eigen berulang. Oleh itu, dengan menguatkuasakan ortogonaliti dengan keadaan eigen yang sepadan dengan $\\lambda_0$, kita sebenarnya mengoptimumkan ke atas subruang yang sepadan dengan nilai eigen selebihnya $\\{\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2,..., \\lambda_{N-1}\\}$. Di sini, $\\lambda_1$ adalah nilai eigen terendah daripada nilai eigen selebihnya dan, oleh itu, penyelesaian optimum bagi masalah baharu boleh diperoleh menggunakan teorem variasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The general idea behind VQD is to use VQE as usual to obtain the lowest eigenvalue $\\lambda_0 := C_0(\\vec\\theta^0) \\equiv C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec\\theta^0)$ along with the corresponding (approximate) eigenstate $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ for some optimal parameter vector $\\vec{\\theta^0}$. Then, to obtain the next eigenvalue $\\lambda_1 > \\lambda_0$, instead of minimizing the cost function $C_0(\\vec{\\theta}) := \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$, we optimize:\n"
msgstr "Idea umum di sebalik VQD adalah menggunakan VQE seperti biasa untuk mendapatkan nilai eigen terendah $\\lambda_0 := C_0(\\vec\\theta^0) \\equiv C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec\\theta^0)$ bersama-sama dengan keadaan eigen (anggaran) yang sepadan $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ untuk beberapa vektor parameter optimum $\\vec{\\theta^0}$. Kemudian, untuk mendapatkan nilai eigen seterusnya $\\lambda_1 > \\lambda_0$, bukannya meminimumkan fungsi kos $C_0(\\vec{\\theta}) := \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$, kita mengoptimumkan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_0(\\vec{\\theta})+ \\beta_0 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_0(\\vec{\\theta})+ \\beta_0 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The positive value $\\beta_0$ should ideally be greater than $\\lambda_1-\\lambda_0$.\n"
msgstr "Nilai positif $\\beta_0$ seharusnya lebih besar daripada $\\lambda_1-\\lambda_0$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This introduces a new cost function that can be viewed as a constrained problem, where we minimize $C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ subject to the constraint that the state must be orthogonal to the previously obtained $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$, with $\\beta_0$ acting as a penalty term if the constraint is not satisfied.\n"
msgstr "Ini memperkenalkan fungsi kos baharu yang boleh dilihat sebagai masalah terkekang, di mana kita meminimumkan $C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ tertakluk kepada kekangan bahawa keadaan mestilah ortogon kepada $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ yang diperoleh sebelum ini, dengan $\\beta_0$ bertindak sebagai sebutan penalti jika kekangan tidak dipenuhi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, this new problem can be interpreted as running VQE on the new observable:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai alternatif, masalah baharu ini boleh ditafsirkan sebagai menjalankan VQE pada observable baharu:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_1} := \\hat{H} + \\beta_0 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_1} := \\hat{H} + \\beta_0 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assuming that the solution to the new problem is $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$, the expected value of $\\hat{H}$ (not $\\hat{H_1}$) should be $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle = \\lambda_1$.\n"
"To obtain the third eigenvalue $\\lambda_2$, the cost function to optimize is:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan mengandaikan bahawa penyelesaian kepada masalah baharu adalah $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$, nilai jangkaan bagi $\\hat{H}$ (bukan $\\hat{H_1}$) haruslah $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle = \\lambda_1$.\n"
"Untuk mendapatkan nilai eigen ketiga $\\lambda_2$, fungsi kos yang perlu dioptimumkan adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_1 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_1 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\beta_1$ is a positive constant large enough to enforce orthogonality of the solution state to both $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ and $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$. This penalizes states in the search space that do not meet this requirement, effectively restricting the search space. Thus, the optimal solution of the new problem should be the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_2$.\n"
msgstr "di mana $\\beta_1$ adalah pemalar positif yang cukup besar untuk menguatkuasakan ortogonaliti keadaan penyelesaian kepada kedua-dua $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ dan $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$. Ini menghukum keadaan dalam ruang carian yang tidak memenuhi keperluan ini, secara berkesan menyekat ruang carian. Oleh itu, penyelesaian optimum bagi masalah baharu haruslah keadaan eigen yang sepadan dengan $\\lambda_2$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Like the previous case, this new problem can also be interpreted as VQE with the observable:\n"
msgstr "Seperti kes sebelumnya, masalah baharu ini juga boleh ditafsirkan sebagai VQE dengan observable:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_2} := \\hat{H_1} + \\beta_1 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_2} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_2} := \\hat{H_1} + \\beta_1 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_2} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the solution to this new problem is $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle$, the expected value of $\\hat{H}$ (not $\\hat{H_2}$) should be $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle = \\lambda_2$.\n"
"Analogously, to obtain the $k$-th eigenvalue $\\lambda_{k-1}$, you would minimize the cost function:\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika penyelesaian kepada masalah baharu ini adalah $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle$, nilai jangkaan bagi $\\hat{H}$ (bukan $\\hat{H_2}$) haruslah $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle = \\lambda_2$.\n"
"Secara analog, untuk mendapatkan nilai eigen ke-$k$ iaitu $\\lambda_{k-1}$, anda akan meminimumkan fungsi kos:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_{k-2}(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_{k-2} |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle  |^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_{k-2}(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_{k-2} |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle  |^2,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember that we defined $\\vec{\\theta^j}$ such that $\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle = \\lambda_j, \\forall j<k$. This problem is equivalent to minimizing $C(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ but with the constraint that the state must be orthogonal to $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle ; \\forall j \\in {0, \\cdots, k-1}$, thereby restricting the search space to the subspace corresponding to the eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_{k-1},\\cdots,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Ingat bahawa kita mendefinisikan $\\vec{\\theta^j}$ sedemikian sehingga $\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle = \\lambda_j, \\forall j<k$. Masalah ini bersamaan dengan meminimumkan $C(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ tetapi dengan kekangan bahawa keadaan mestilah ortogon kepada $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle ; \\forall j \\in {0, \\cdots, k-1}$, dengan itu menyekat ruang carian kepada subruang yang sepadan dengan nilai eigen $\\{\\lambda_{k-1},\\cdots,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This problem is equivalent to a VQE with the observable:\n"
msgstr "Masalah ini bersamaan dengan VQE dengan observable:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-1} :=\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-2} + \\beta_{k-2} |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H}_{k-1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-1} :=\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-2} + \\beta_{k-2} |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H}_{k-1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As you can see from the process, to obtain the $k$-th eigenvalue, you need the (approximate) eigenstates of the previous $k-1$ eigenvalues, so you would need to run VQE a total of $k$ times. Therefore, VQD's cost function is as follows:\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang anda dapat lihat dari proses ini, untuk mendapatkan nilai eigen ke-$k$, anda memerlukan keadaan eigen (anggaran) bagi $k-1$ nilai eigen sebelumnya, jadi anda perlu menjalankan VQE sebanyak $k$ kali. Oleh itu, fungsi kos VQD adalah seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_k(\\vec{\\theta}) =\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_k(\\vec{\\theta}) =\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout-2}"
msgstr "Susun atur teori {#theoretical-layout-2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "VQD's layout can be summarized as follows:\n"
msgstr "Susun atur VQD boleh diringkaskan seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare a reference operator $U_R$\n"
msgstr "Sediakan operator rujukan $U_R$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to the reference state, creating the following ansatze $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$\n"
msgstr "Gunakan bentuk variasi $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ kepada keadaan rujukan, mencipta ansatz berikut $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bootstrap at $i=0$ if we have a similar problem (typically found via classical simulation or sampling).\n"
msgstr "Bootstrap pada $i=0$ jika kita mempunyai masalah yang serupa (biasanya ditemui melalui simulasi atau pensampelan klasik).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate the cost function $C_k(\\vec{\\theta})$, which involves computing $k$ excited states and an array of $\\beta$'s defining the overlap penalty for each overlap term.\n"
msgstr "Nilaikan fungsi kos $C_k(\\vec{\\theta})$, yang melibatkan pengiraan $k$ keadaan teruja dan tatasusunan $\\beta$ yang mentakrifkan penalti pertindanan untuk setiap sebutan pertindanan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the expectation value for an observable $\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ for each $k$\n"
msgstr "Kira nilai jangkaan bagi observable $\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ untuk setiap $k$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the penalty $\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2$.\n"
msgstr "Kira penalti $\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cost function should then return the sum of these two terms\n"
msgstr "Fungsi kos kemudian harus mengembalikan jumlah kedua-dua sebutan ini\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use a classical optimizer to choose the next set of parameters $\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan pengoptimum klasik untuk memilih set parameter seterusnya $\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat this process until convergence is reached.\n"
msgstr "Ulang proses ini sehingga penumpuan dicapai.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation {#implementation-1}"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan {#implementation-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this implementation, we'll create a function for an overlap penalty. This penalty will be used in the cost function at each iteration. This process will be repeated for each excited state\n"
msgstr "Untuk pelaksanaan ini, kita akan membuat fungsi untuk penalti pertindihan. Penalti ini akan digunakan dalam fungsi kos pada setiap lelaran. Proses ini akan diulang untuk setiap keadaan teruja.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/extracted-outputs/9d368de5-d512-4fe8-8842-9c735944b22b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/extracted-outputs/9d368de5-d512-4fe8-8842-9c735944b22b-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we'll set up a function that calculates the state fidelity -- a percentage of overlap between two states that we'll use as a penalty for VQD:\n"
msgstr "Pertama, kita akan menyediakan fungsi yang mengira kesetiaan keadaan — peratusan pertindihan antara dua keadaan yang akan kita gunakan sebagai penalti untuk VQD:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It's time to write VQD's cost function. As before when we calculated only the ground state, we will determine the lowest energy state using the Estimator primitive. However, as described above, we will now add a penalty term to ensure orthogonality of higher-energy states. That is, for each new excited state, a penalty is added for any overlap between the current variational state and the lower-energy eigenstates already found.\n"
msgstr "Tiba masanya untuk menulis fungsi kos VQD. Seperti sebelum ini ketika kita mengira hanya keadaan asas, kita akan menentukan keadaan tenaga terendah menggunakan primitif Estimator. Namun, seperti yang diterangkan di atas, kita kini akan menambah penalti untuk memastikan ortogonaliti keadaan bertenaga lebih tinggi. Iaitu, bagi setiap keadaan teruja baharu, satu penalti ditambah untuk sebarang pertindihan antara keadaan variasi semasa dan eigenstate bertenaga lebih rendah yang telah dijumpai.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note especially that the cost function above refers to the `calculate_overlaps` function, which actually creates a new quantum circuit. If we want to run on real hardware, that new circuit must also be transpiled, hopefully in an optimal way, to run on the backend we select. Note that transpilation has been built in to the `calculate_overlaps` or `cost_func_vqd` functions. Feel free to try modifying the code yourself to build in this additional (and conditional) transpilation - but this will also be done for you in the next lesson.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan terutamanya bahawa fungsi kos di atas merujuk kepada fungsi `calculate_overlaps`, yang sebenarnya mencipta Circuit kuantum baharu. Jika kita ingin menjalankan pada perkakasan sebenar, Circuit baharu itu juga perlu ditranspilasi, sebaik-baiknya dengan cara yang optimum, untuk dijalankan pada Backend yang kita pilih. Perhatikan bahawa transpilasi belum dibina ke dalam fungsi `calculate_overlaps` atau `cost_func_vqd`. Sila cuba ubah suai kod sendiri untuk membina transpilasi tambahan (dan bersyarat) ini — tetapi ini juga akan dilakukan untuk anda dalam pelajaran seterusnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this lesson, we will run the VQD algorithm using the Statevector Sampler and Statevector Estimator:\n"
msgstr "Dalam pelajaran ini, kita akan menjalankan algoritma VQD menggunakan Statevector Sampler dan Statevector Estimator:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will introduce an observable to be estimated. In the next lesson we will add some physical context to this, like the excited state of a molecule. It may be helpful to think of this observable as the Hamiltonian of a system that can have excited states, even though this observable has not been chosen to match any particular molecule or atom.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan memperkenalkan observable yang perlu dianggarkan. Dalam pelajaran seterusnya kita akan menambah konteks fizikal kepada ini, seperti keadaan teruja molekul. Mungkin berguna untuk memikirkan observable ini sebagai Hamiltonian bagi suatu sistem yang boleh mempunyai keadaan teruja, walaupun observable ini tidak dipilih untuk sepadan dengan mana-mana molekul atau atom tertentu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, we set the total number of states we wish to calculate (ground state and excited states, k), and the penalties (betas) for overlap between statevectors that should be orthogonal. The consequences of choosing betas to be too high or too low will be explored a bit in the next lesson. For now, we will simply use those provided below. We will start by using all zeros as our parameters. In your own calculations, you may want to use more clever starting parameters based on your knowledge of the system or on previous calculations.\n"
msgstr "Di sini, kita menetapkan jumlah keadaan yang ingin dikira (keadaan asas dan keadaan teruja, k), serta penalti (betas) untuk pertindihan antara vektor keadaan yang sepatutnya ortogonal. Akibat memilih betas yang terlalu tinggi atau terlalu rendah akan diterokai sedikit dalam pelajaran seterusnya. Buat masa ini, kita akan menggunakan nilai yang diberikan di bawah sahaja. Kita akan bermula dengan menggunakan semua sifar sebagai parameter kita. Dalam pengiraan anda sendiri, anda mungkin ingin menggunakan parameter permulaan yang lebih bijak berdasarkan pengetahuan anda tentang sistem atau pengiraan sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now run the calculation:\n"
msgstr "Kita kini boleh menjalankan pengiraan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The values we obtained from the cost function are approximately -6.00, 4.02, and 5.61. The important thing about these results is that the function values are increasing. If we had obtained a first excited state that is lower in energy than our initial, unconstrained calculation of the ground state, that would have indicated an error somewhere in our code.\n"
msgstr "Nilai yang kita perolehi daripada fungsi kos adalah lebih kurang -6.00, 4.02, dan 5.61. Perkara penting tentang keputusan ini ialah nilai fungsi semakin meningkat. Jika kita mendapat keadaan teruja pertama yang lebih rendah tenaganya daripada pengiraan awal tanpa kekangan bagi keadaan asas, itu akan menunjukkan terdapat ralat di suatu tempat dalam kod kita.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The values of x are the parameters that yielded a statevector corresponding to each of these costs (energies).\n"
msgstr "Nilai x adalah parameter yang menghasilkan vektor keadaan yang sepadan dengan setiap kos (tenaga) ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we note that all three minimizations converged to within the default tolerance of the classical optimizer (here COBYLA). They required 131, 110, and 90 function evaluations, respectively.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, kita perhatikan bahawa ketiga-tiga penganggitan minimum telah menumpu dalam toleransi lalai pengoptimum klasik (di sini COBYLA). Ia memerlukan 131, 110, dan 90 penilaian fungsi masing-masing.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum Sampling Regression (QSR) {#quantum-sampling-regression-qsr}"
msgstr "Regresi Pensampelan Kuantum (QSR) {#quantum-sampling-regression-qsr}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One of the main issues with VQE is the multiple calls to a quantum computer that are required to obtain the parameters for each step, for example, $k$, $k-1$, and so on. This is especially problematic when access to quantum devices is queued. While a [`Session`](/guides/run-jobs-session) can be used to group multiple iterative calls, an alternative approach is to use sampling. By utilizing more classical resources, we can complete the full optimization process in a single call. This is where [Quantum Sampling Regression](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.02338) comes into play. Since access to quantum computers is still a low-offer/high-demand commodity, we find this trade-off to be both possible and convenient for many current studies. This approach harnesses all available classical capabilities while still capturing many of the inner workings and intrinsic properties of quantum computations that do not appear in simulation.\n"
msgstr "Salah satu isu utama dengan VQE ialah banyaknya panggilan kepada komputer kuantum yang diperlukan untuk mendapatkan parameter bagi setiap langkah, contohnya $k$, $k-1$, dan seterusnya. Ini amat bermasalah apabila akses kepada peranti kuantum mempunyai giliran. Walaupun [`Session`](/guides/run-jobs-session) boleh digunakan untuk mengumpulkan pelbagai panggilan berulang, pendekatan alternatif ialah menggunakan pensampelan. Dengan memanfaatkan lebih banyak sumber klasik, kita boleh melengkapkan keseluruhan proses pengoptimuman dalam satu panggilan sahaja. Di sinilah [Regresi Pensampelan Kuantum](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.02338) memainkan peranannya. Memandangkan akses kepada komputer kuantum masih merupakan komoditi tawaran rendah/permintaan tinggi, kita mendapati pertukaran ini adalah mungkin dan mudah untuk banyak kajian semasa. Pendekatan ini memanfaatkan semua keupayaan klasik yang ada sambil masih menangkap banyak mekanisme dalaman dan sifat intrinsik pengiraan kuantum yang tidak muncul dalam simulasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing how QSR uses the components of a variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-qsr.svg)\n"
msgstr "![A diagram showing how QSR uses the components of a variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-qsr.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The idea behind QSR is that the cost function $C(\\theta) := \\langle \\psi(\\theta) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\theta)\\rangle$ can be expressed as a Fourier series in the following manner:\n"
msgstr "Idea di sebalik QSR ialah fungsi kos $C(\\theta) := \\langle \\psi(\\theta) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\theta)\\rangle$ boleh dinyatakan sebagai siri Fourier dengan cara berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& := \\langle \\psi(\\theta) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\theta)\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& := \\langle \\psi(\\theta) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\theta)\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& := a_0 + \\sum_{k=1}^S[a_k\\cos(k\\theta)+ b_k\\sin(k\\theta)] \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& := a_0 + \\sum_{k=1}^S[a_k\\cos(k\\theta)+ b_k\\sin(k\\theta)] \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Depending on the periodicity and bandwidth of the original function, the set $S$ may be finite or infinite. For the purposes of this discussion, we will assume it is infinite. The next step is to sample the cost function $C(\\theta)$ multiple times in order to obtain the Fourier coefficients $\\{a_0, a_k, b_k\\}_{k=1}^S$. Specifically, since we have $2S+1$ unknowns, we will need to sample the cost function $2S+1$ times.\n"
msgstr "Bergantung pada kekerapan dan lebar jalur fungsi asal, set $S$ mungkin terhingga atau tak terhingga. Untuk tujuan perbincangan ini, kita akan menganggapnya tak terhingga. Langkah seterusnya ialah mengsampel fungsi kos $C(\\theta)$ beberapa kali untuk mendapatkan pekali Fourier $\\{a_0, a_k, b_k\\}_{k=1}^S$. Khususnya, oleh kerana kita mempunyai $2S+1$ yang tidak diketahui, kita perlu mengsampel fungsi kos sebanyak $2S+1$ kali.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we then sample the cost function for $2S+1$ parameter values $\\{\\theta_1,...,\\theta_{2S+1}\\}$, we can obtain the following system:\n"
msgstr "Jika kita kemudian mengsampel fungsi kos untuk $2S+1$ nilai parameter $\\{\\theta_1,...,\\theta_{2S+1}\\}$, kita boleh mendapatkan sistem berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & \\cos(\\theta_1) & \\sin(\\theta_1) & \\cos(2\\theta_1) & ... & \\sin(S\\theta_1) \\\\\n"
"1 & \\cos(\\theta_2) & \\sin(\\theta_2) & \\cos(2\\theta_2) & \\cdots & \\sin(S\\theta_2)\\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\\n"
"1 & \\cos(\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\sin(\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\cos(2\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\cdots & \\sin(S\\theta_{2S+1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} a_0 \\\\ a_1 \\\\ b_1 \\\\ a_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ b_S \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} C(\\theta_1) \\\\ C(\\theta_2) \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ C(\\theta_{2S+1}) \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & \\cos(\\theta_1) & \\sin(\\theta_1) & \\cos(2\\theta_1) & ... & \\sin(S\\theta_1) \\\\\n"
"1 & \\cos(\\theta_2) & \\sin(\\theta_2) & \\cos(2\\theta_2) & \\cdots & \\sin(S\\theta_2)\\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\\n"
"1 & \\cos(\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\sin(\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\cos(2\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\cdots & \\sin(S\\theta_{2S+1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} a_0 \\\\ a_1 \\\\ b_1 \\\\ a_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ b_S \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} C(\\theta_1) \\\\ C(\\theta_2) \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ C(\\theta_{2S+1}) \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "that we'll rewrite as\n"
msgstr "yang akan kita tulis semula sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Fa=c.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Fa=c.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In practice, this system is generally not consistent because the cost function values $c$ are not exact. Therefore, it is usually a good idea to normalize them by multiplying them by $F^\\dagger$ on the left, which results in:\n"
msgstr "Dalam amalan, sistem ini biasanya tidak konsisten kerana nilai fungsi kos $c$ tidak tepat. Oleh itu, biasanya adalah idea yang baik untuk menormalkannya dengan mendarabkan dengan $F^\\dagger$ di sebelah kiri, yang menghasilkan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"F^\\dagger Fa = F^\\dagger c.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"F^\\dagger Fa = F^\\dagger c.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This new system is always consistent, and its solution is a least-squares solution to the original problem. If we have $k$ parameters instead of just one, and each parameter $\\theta^i$ has its own $S_i$ for $i \\in {1,...,k}$, then the total number of samples required is:\n"
msgstr "Sistem baharu ini sentiasa konsisten, dan penyelesaiannya adalah penyelesaian kuasa dua terkecil bagi masalah asal. Jika kita mempunyai $k$ parameter dan bukannya satu sahaja, dan setiap parameter $\\theta^i$ mempunyai $S_i$ sendiri untuk $i \\in {1,...,k}$, maka jumlah sampel yang diperlukan ialah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"T=\\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_i+1)\\leq \\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_{max}+1) = (2S_{max}+1)^n,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"T=\\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_i+1)\\leq \\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_{max}+1) = (2S_{max}+1)^n,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $S_{\\max} = \\max_i(S_i)$. Furthermore, adjusting $S_{\\max}$ as a tunable parameter (instead of inferring it) opens up new possibilities, such as:\n"
msgstr "di mana $S_{\\max} = \\max_i(S_i)$. Tambahan pula, melaraskan $S_{\\max}$ sebagai parameter boleh ditala (dan bukannya menyimpulkannya) membuka kemungkinan baharu, seperti:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Over-sampling** to improve accuracy.\n"
msgstr "**Pensampelan berlebihan** untuk meningkatkan ketepatan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Under-sampling** to boost performance by reducing runtime overhead or eliminating local minima.\n"
msgstr "**Pensampelan kurang** untuk meningkatkan prestasi dengan mengurangkan overhed masa jalan atau menghapuskan minimum tempatan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout-3}"
msgstr "Susun atur teori {#theoretical-layout-3}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "QSR's layout can be summarized as follows:\n"
msgstr "Susun atur QSR boleh dirumuskan seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare reference operators $U_R$.\n"
msgstr "Sediakan pengendali rujukan $U_R$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll go from the state $|0\\rangle$ to the reference state $|\\rho\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "Kita akan pergi dari keadaan $|0\\rangle$ ke keadaan rujukan $|\\rho\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply the  variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to create an ansatz $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan bentuk variasi $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ untuk mencipta ansatz $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Determine the bandwidth associated with each parameter in the ansatz. An upper bound is sufficient.\n"
msgstr "Tentukan lebar jalur yang berkaitan dengan setiap parameter dalam ansatz. Batas atas sudah mencukupi.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bootstrap at $i=0$ if we have a similar problem (typically found by classical simulation or sampling).\n"
msgstr "Bootstrap pada $i=0$ jika kita mempunyai masalah yang serupa (biasanya dijumpai melalui simulasi klasik atau pensampelan).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample the cost function $C(\\vec\\theta) := a_0 + \\sum_{k=1}^S[a_k\\cos(k\\theta)+ b_k\\sin(k\\theta)]$ at least $T$ times.\n"
msgstr "Sampel fungsi kos $C(\\vec\\theta) := a_0 + \\sum_{k=1}^S[a_k\\cos(k\\theta)+ b_k\\sin(k\\theta)]$ sekurang-kurangnya $T$ kali.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$T=\\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_i+1)\\leq \\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_{max}+1) = (2S_{max}+1)^n$\n"
msgstr "$T=\\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_i+1)\\leq \\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_{max}+1) = (2S_{max}+1)^n$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Decide whether to over-sample/under-sample to balance speed vs accuracy by adjusting $T$.\n"
msgstr "Tentukan sama ada perlu pensampelan berlebihan/kurang untuk mengimbangi kelajuan vs ketepatan dengan melaraskan $T$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute the Fourier coefficients from the samples (that is, solve the normalized linear system of equations).\n"
msgstr "Kira pekali Fourier daripada sampel (iaitu, selesaikan sistem persamaan linear yang dinormalkan).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solve for the global minimum of the resulting regression function on a classical machine.\n"
msgstr "Selesaikan minimum global bagi fungsi regresi yang terhasil pada mesin klasik.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Ringkasan {#summary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With this lesson, you learned about multiple variational instances available:\n"
msgstr "Dengan pelajaran ini, anda telah belajar tentang pelbagai contoh variasi yang tersedia:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "General layout\n"
msgstr "Susun atur umum\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introducing weights and penalties to adjust a cost function\n"
msgstr "Memperkenalkan pemberat dan penalti untuk melaraskan fungsi kos\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exploring under-sampling vs over-sampling to trade-off speed vs accuracy\n"
msgstr "Meneroka pensampelan kurang vs pensampelan berlebihan untuk menukar kelajuan vs ketepatan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These ideas can be adapted to form a custom variational algorithm that fits your problem. We encourage you to share your results with the community. The next lesson will explore how to use a variational algorithm to solve an application.\n"
msgstr "Idea-idea ini boleh disesuaikan untuk membentuk algoritma variasi tersuai yang sesuai dengan masalah anda. Kami menggalakkan anda berkongsi hasil anda dengan komuniti. Pelajaran seterusnya akan meneroka cara menggunakan algoritma variasi untuk menyelesaikan suatu aplikasi.\n"
